[4b] (BAND-EQ) -- the ONE sentence that is left.  A band-carrying gap-1 parent has
     A[1]=...=A[d+1]=c > A[d+2].  By Theorem GAP1 its outcome is EQ iff c = u+1 where
     u is the level of the second raised index i0.  Since u <= A[d+2] <= c-1, EQ is
     EXACTLY 'A[d+2] = c-1 and i0 sits at that level'.  Measured inside and outside
     the family, so that the family-side content is separated from the general fact.
     band-carrying gap-1 parents in P1+P2 : 100
     (does the entry past the band sit at c-1 ?, is the raised level c-1 ?) : {('A[d+2]=c-1', 'u=c-1'): 100}
     position of i0 for those parents      : {'i0>d+1': 100}
     SAME configuration OUTSIDE the family (W+zeros), (raised level, outcome) : {"('u<=c-2', 'UNIT_DOWN')": 54, "('u=c-1', 'EQ')": 336}
    [ok] CONTROL: band-carrying gap-1 parents exist inside P1+P2                              hits=100
    [ok] CORRUPT CONTROL: outside the family the band DOES reach GAP1's UNIT_DOWN branch      hits=54

