[9] (PIVOT-MAJ) vs (DOM-MAJ).  p(.) dominance is TRANSITIVE, so if every dominance
    pair (A,B) of TERMINATING partitions of N is joined by a chain of SINGLE unit
    transfers down that stays inside the terminating partitions, then
    (PIVOT-MAJ) => (DOM-MAJ) outright and r44's 'better-shaped' census is the SAME
    statement, not a stronger one.  The obstruction is that a unit transfer can leave
    the terminating set -- (3,3,1,1) ABORTS (r44's E05 audit).  Measured per N.
    dominance pairs of terminating partitions tested : 7403
